      {
        "id": 85017,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-22T21:41:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I played Fanatic last night to good effect, although I didn't really follow this advice.&nbsp; I was not especially conservative, but I didn't go crazy either.&nbsp; Absolution came out on turn 1, so I didn't Exorcise until very late in the game when I Emboldened myself...I always prefer to Embolden others if possible.&nbsp; I had a lot of little plinking cards which I played every turn, and I completely ignored Zealous Offense because we were playing against Plague Rat (there were Environment targets, but why bother).&nbsp; Consecrated Ground is great.&nbsp; No Aegis, no Wrath, no Martyr, no End of Days.&nbsp; I rather liked the version of her I was getting this time.&nbsp; Usually I'm not so lucky.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
